## Steps

1. Call **Attempt_Chat_Get**(chat_entry_id: "{{ params.chat_id }}", draft_id: "{{ params.draft_id }}", attempt_id: "{{ params.attempt_id }}")
2. From the response, collect resource IDs from **Available** sections only:
   - `personas_ids` — all available persona IDs
   - `objectives_ids` — all available objective IDs (if section shown)
   - `problem_statements_ids` — exactly 1 problem statement ID (if section shown)
   - `questions_ids` — all available question IDs (if section shown)
   - `documents_ids` — all available document IDs
   - `images_ids` — at most 1 image ID (if section shown)
   - `videos_ids` — at most 1 video ID (if section shown)
   - `options_ids` — all available option IDs (if section shown)
   - **Skip** any section marked "Selected (locked)" — those are already set
   - **Skip** any section not shown — it's disabled
   - **Never pass** `scenarios_ids` or `departments_ids` — they are auto-configured
3. Call **Attempt_Chat_Create** with:
   - `attempt_id`: `"{{ params.attempt_id }}"`
   - `chat_id`: `"{{ params.chat_id }}"`
   - `text_enabled`: `true`
   - All the resource IDs collected in step 2 (only from Available sections)
4. Call **Attempt_Group**(group_id: "{{ group_id }}", name: "short descriptive name")

**IMPORTANT:**
- Use `chat_id: "{{ params.chat_id }}"` and `attempt_id: "{{ params.attempt_id }}"` exactly — do NOT substitute the draft_id
- Only pass IDs from **Available** sections — locked and hidden sections are handled automatically
- If a resource section has no Available items, omit that field
